      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'll dispute that it's important to bypass audio limits. a max-volume explosion is loud enough. wanting a high dynamic range is one thing, giving everyone else a high dynamic range they didn't ask for is another. However, phase syncing audio is a very inefficient way of increasing volume, since perceived volume is logarithmic, every percentage increase requires exponentially more audio sources. I can understand what they're going for, but this is a really, really bad way of going about it if it's true.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
